A47 — take `-r` as the grid, not as the mode's refresh

`-r` is the session's vblank grid, while the panel's real rate is what the DRM
mode advertises. `init_drm` hands the grid to `preferred_refresh`, and the mode
search requires `mode->vrefresh` to equal it, so a grid that matches no mode
falls through to the first mode on the connector — with `-r 1200` it matches
nothing.

The lookup now re-finds by the requested size with the refresh unconstrained, so
the nested refresh is free to differ from the mode's rate and a connector whose
modes all carry the real rate still yields an output.

This is the second half of the old A34, kept when A34's fps cap was parked: the
cap no longer exists, but the grid argument does.

--- a/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
+++ b/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
@@ -1385,6 +1385,16 @@
 		mode = find_mode(best->GetModeConnector(), drm->preferred_width, drm->preferred_height, gamescope::ConvertmHzToHz( drm->preferred_refresh ));
 	}
 
+	// gamenative A47: -r is the session's vblank grid, not the mode's rate: the
+	// panel's real refresh is what the connector advertises, so the grid matches
+	// no mode. Re-find by size alone rather than let the grid pick the mode, so
+	// the nested refresh is free to differ from the mode's rate and a connector
+	// whose only modes carry the real rate still yields an output.
+	if (!mode && drm->preferred_refresh != 0)
+	{
+		mode = find_mode(best->GetModeConnector(), drm->preferred_width, drm->preferred_height, 0);
+	}
+
 	if (!mode && best->GetScreenType() == gamescope::GAMESCOPE_SCREEN_TYPE_EXTERNAL) {
 		saved_mode mode_info{};
 		if (get_saved_mode(description, mode_info))
